ibrahim says he'll never forget the day  a car bomb nearly killed him  he says his shattered legs were gushing  blood  he's a mechanic in somalia's capital  mogadishu you know  it was in the morning when a client  brought me his car for repairing as soon  as i started working on it the car blew  up because it had a bomb attached and i  didn't know about it  he's here in the street right outside of  tosh's home that him and other mechanics  work on tuk-tuks cars and bikes and it's  right here that the bomb went off  he would have joined the other hundreds  of somalis who died in armed conflict  every year if it wasn't for one man  dr ahmed abdul qadeer mohammed says he  was tired of seeing people bleed to  death so he set up somalia's only public  blood bank funded by private donors  this is what inspired him five years ago  about 600 people were killed when two  truck bombs exploded in mogadishu it was  the worst attack in somalia's history  investigators blamed the armed group  al-shabab many of those killed bled to  death from their injuries  dr ahmed decided to do something about  it  it feels like the country is in an  emergency all the time with many  explosions and accidents there is always  a need for blood this center supplies  blood to many hospitals in the city to  save the lives of wounded people mothers  in childbirth and others  atosh is one of the many people who've  been saved with the blood that dr ahmed  collects  he and his team deliver it to hospitals  where it's needed  he says more people die of blood loss  than from the bullets that hit them and  the un says about 5 000 women die in  childbirth in somalia every year  many of whom could be saved by blood  transfusions  moalim  is another one of the blood recipients  he says a doctor misdiagnosed him with  tuberculosis and gave him strong drugs  that destroyed his kidneys he now  depends on kidney dialysis with donated  blood  it's a good thing for the community  without him so many people would be  dying because of lack of blood like me  if i did not get blood from him it would  be hard for me to stay alive  dr ahmed says finding donors is hard he  says he's met many people who believe  they'll die if they donate he speaks on  tv and radio every week to educate and  encourage people  the bank stores enough blood to treat  just a few hundred patients it's a start  but he says he has a long way to go to  meet somalia's needs  malcolm webb al jazeera mogadishu  somalia
 

